<title>USA: U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. rice major sales activity in the week ended Sept 5 reported by exporters for the following purchasing countries, in tonnes:</p>
<p>Net Sales:	1996/97		 1997/98</p>
<p> Spain	     6,000-A		 Nil</p>
<p> Netherlands     3,900</p>
<p> Saudi Arabia    3,700</p>
<p> Mexico	    3,000-B</p>
<p> Japan	     2,900</p>
<p> Honduras	  2,500-C</p>
<p>A- all rough.</p>
<p>B- includes 2,600 tonnes of rough rice.</p>
<p>C- includes 2,200 tonnes of rough rice.</p>
<p>Net sales of 28,300 tonnes were 23 percent below the prior week and 5 percent lower than the four-week average.</p>
<p>Weekly exports of 37,800 tonnes were 44 percent lower than a week earlier but 16 percent up from the four-week average.</p>
<p>Primary Export Destinations: Philippines, Netherlands, Canada, Honduras and Trinidad.</p>
</text>
